Whitecube Trainer standalone package
===================================

The upstream NOTICE covers the full Whitecube repository. This standalone
package contains Trainer, its pipeline, a pinned private Parquet decoder, the
GTK theme and trainer icon.
It does not bundle the compositor, Electron, wlroots, cairo or other apps.

Launch Whitecube Trainer from your applications menu or run:

    whitecube-trainer
    whitecube-trainer-cli --help
    whitecube-trainer-cli --doctor

The standalone commands deliberately differ from cube-train and whitecube-train
provided by whitecube-desktop, so the packages can coexist without overwriting
one another. No Whitecube compositor or desktop session is required. GTK uses
your current Wayland or X11 desktop and honors GDK_BACKEND when explicitly set.

Training runtime
----------------
Inspect needs neither Torch nor NumPy in the selected training environment.
Prepare-only uses system Python and its required NumPy package without Torch.
Normal training uses the selected Torch environment; Parquet decoding can use
the separate system/private decoder in each workflow.

The desktop never imports PyTorch. Select a Python interpreter in Train, then
use Check runtime. NumPy is a required dependency for corpus preparation; the
recommended python3-torch package provides a system CPU training runtime. Existing CUDA virtual environments can be selected
instead. Parquet decoding is independent of the selected training environment:
Debian 13 uses the included CPython 3.13 PyArrow runtime; systems providing
python3-pyarrow use their system Python decoder. The dependency alternative is
python3.13 | python3-pyarrow. safetensors remains optional for weights export,
and Jupyter/ipykernel for notebook execution. Nothing is downloaded by package
maintainer scripts; this package has no maintainer scripts.

GTK >= 4.12 and libadwaita >= 1.5 are required. Older distributions must upgrade
these libraries before this package can be installed.

User data
---------
Runs default to ~/train-out (override WHITECUBE_TRAIN_OUT). Preferences are in
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/whitecube/trainer.json, with ~/.config as the default.
Jobs use $XDG_STATE_HOME/whitecube/trainer, with ~/.local/state as the default.
Removing the package preserves runs, environments and settings.

Rebuilding
----------
From apps/cube-train:

    ./packaging/build-deb.sh

Output goes to dist/whitecube-trainer_<version>_amd64.deb with a SHA256 sidecar.
--output-dir, --version and --epoch are supported. SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH or the
repository's latest commit timestamp makes identical source builds reproducible.
The build requires Python 3, git, dpkg, dpkg-deb, dpkg-shlibdeps, readelf and ldd.
It downloads the exact PyArrow wheel recorded in packaging/parquet-runtime.json
when absent from the local cache and verifies its SHA256 before extraction.
The wheel is never installed into host Python. No compilation, host package
installation or privileged action is performed. The amd64 architecture and
interpreter dependency reflect the bundled native extension ABI. All upstream
licenses and notices remain in parquet-runtime/pyarrow-26.0.0.dist-info/licenses/.
